      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Economic Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana is a dominant contributor to India's central pool of foodgrains, specifically wheat and basmati rice.",
        "Gurugram and Faridabad serve as the industrial and automotive manufacturing engines of the state.",
        "The tertiary sector, dominated by IT and financial services in the National Capital Region (NCR), is a major driver of the state's economy.",
        "Key national research centers, including the National Dairy Research Institute (NDRI), are located in Karnal and Hisar."
      ],
      "id": "tfzfeq0"
    },
